{
 "_file": "harness/costmodel/layer_chunks.json",
 "_purpose": "What `key_tile.py --selftest` checks the boundary form and the whole-chunk identity against: every chunk of one token block of each headline run, layer chunks and output-head chunks alike, so the check runs with no artifacts directory and no path into another repository.",
 "_source": "Copied from the zk-results run outputs each point names: `runs/<run>/<output>`, `result.chunks[]`. `fresh`, `base` and `interaction` are the chunk's own `cells`; `key_tiles` and `key_tiles_interaction` are `family_cells.key_tiles` and `family_cells.interaction_by_family.key_tiles.cells`; `table_rows` is the sum of `2^log_rows` over `family_cells.tables`. Nothing is derived and nothing is rounded.",
 "_shape": "`shape` is what every point shares; a point repeats only what differs from it. `head` marks an output-head chunk: it tiles no prefix, publishes no root-equality claim and commits one boundary side, so only the boundary form is checked against it. `embedding` marks layer 0, which carries the embedding lookup and one more cell per attention-output accumulator than every other layer.",
